%% aoneahsan-cccs-firestore — full flow
flowchart TD
    trigger([Firestore work]) --> task{What are you doing?}

    task -->|designing a collection| shape[Model for the QUERY, not the entity —<br/>no joins, no substring search]
    shape --> lists{Will a list view need fields<br/>from another document?}
    lists -->|yes| denorm[Denormalise onto the document.<br/>A fan-out write beats N reads<br/>per render]
    lists -->|no| children
    denorm --> children
    children{Many children, or queried<br/>independently?}
    children -->|yes| subcoll[Subcollection]
    children -->|no| embed[Embed, or use an array<br/>with array-contains]
    subcoll --> search
    embed --> search
    search{Does the feature need<br/>substring or fuzzy search?}
    search -->|yes| notfirestore[Firestore cannot do this.<br/>Move that feature to a database<br/>with real text search]
    search -->|no| query

    task -->|writing a query| query{Is there an explicit limit?}
    query -->|no| bug[BUG — regardless of current size.<br/>Default 20, hard max 50]
    query -->|yes| filtering
    bug --> filtering
    filtering[Filter and sort SERVER-side.<br/>Cursor pagination beyond page 1]
    filtering --> counting{Do you need a count?}
    counting -->|yes| agg["getCountFromServer — one read per<br/>1000 index entries — or a counter<br/>field. NEVER read docs to count them"]
    counting -->|no| audit
    agg --> audit

    task -->|permission or index<br/>error in production| audit
    audit[/🔴 The query to rules to index audit/]
    audit --> record[Record every query in<br/>docs/firestore-queries.json:<br/>collection, operation, fields,<br/>filters, orderBy, composite needs]
    record --> rulecheck{Does a rule allow the<br/>intended access?}
    rulecheck -->|no| writerule[Write it — deny by default,<br/>validate shape and ownership]
    rulecheck -->|yes| idxcheck
    writerule --> idxcheck
    idxcheck{Does a composite index exist<br/>for this filter+sort combination?}
    idxcheck -->|no| addidx[Add it. A new sort on an existing<br/>filter needs a NEW index]
    idxcheck -->|yes| testas
    addidx --> testas

    testas{Who are you testing as?}
    testas -->|an admin| adminttrap[🔴 STOP. An admin passes every<br/>role gate, so rules bugs VANISH.<br/>This masked total production<br/>breakage twice]
    adminttrap --> nonadmin
    testas -->|a plain user| nonadmin[Correct — test as a NON-admin]
    nonadmin --> writefail{Is a write still failing?}
    writefail -->|yes| sideeffect[Suspect the SIDE-EFFECT writes:<br/>counters, tags, audit rows.<br/>The primary doc is often allowed<br/>while a helper write is denied]
    writefail -->|no| deploy
    sideeffect --> deploy

    notfirestore --> deploy
    deploy["Deploy rules and indexes SEPARATELY —<br/>never --only firestore"]
    deploy --> done([Zero permission and index errors<br/>in production])

    classDef gateNode fill:#fff4e6,stroke:#d97706,color:#7c2d12
    classDef terminal fill:#ecfdf5,stroke:#059669,color:#064e3b
    classDef warn fill:#fef2f2,stroke:#dc2626,color:#7f1d1d
    class task,lists,children,search,query,counting,rulecheck,idxcheck,testas,writefail gateNode
    class trigger,done terminal
    class bug,adminttrap,audit warn
